s":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"minimumVertexCover()"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/approximateMinimumDominatingSet(weight:)-6gboe":{"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/approximateminimumdominatingset(weight:)-6gboe","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dominating set of at most H(Δ + 1) times the least weight (Chvátal’s greedy set cover):"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"repeatedly the vertex with the least weight per newly dominated vertex of its closed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbourhood, the least vertex index on ties. Ratios are compared exactly, by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"cross-multiplication. ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once per vertex. O((n + m) log n).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/approximateMinimumDominatingSet(weight:)-6gboe","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"approximateMinimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","title":"approximateMinimumDominatingSet(weight:)"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph"}],"title":"Graph","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumEdgeCover(matching:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumedgecover(matching:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumEdgeCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"matching"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14MatchingModule0A0V","text":"Matching"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">) -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?"}],"title":"minimumEdgeCover(matching:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The same construction from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"matching"},{"type":"text","text":": pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumBipartiteMatching()"},{"type":"text","text":" on a bipartite"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph for O(m √n). Minimum when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"matching"},{"type":"text","text":" is maximum; from any other matching it is still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an edge cover (a vertex covered by an edge added earlier in the pass is skipped). nil when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"some vertex has no edge. O(n + m)."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumEdgeCover(matching:)"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumDominatingSet()":{"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smaller set is; in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges do"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not matter; isolated vertices are in it. Deterministic, but which minimum set it is depends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","title":"minimumDominatingSet()"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover(bipartition:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"bipartition","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bipartition","preciseIdentifier":"s:15BipartiteGraphs11BipartitionV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"title":"minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","abstract":[{"text":"König’s minimum vertex cover of a bipartite graph: from a maximum matching (Hopcroft–Karp on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the sides), Z is the set of vertices reached from the free left vertices by alternating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths, an edge not in the matching from left to right, then the matched edge back; the cover","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is (left ∖ Z) ∪ (right ∩ Z), in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. It is the one minimum cover with the most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left vertices, so it does not depend on the matching. O(m √n).","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"type":"topic","title":"Graph"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumEdgeCover()":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumedgecover()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumEdgeCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?"}],"title":"minimumEdgeCover()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum edge cover (positions, ascending), or nil when some vertex has no edge: the edges of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"maximumMatching()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", then for each vertex still uncovered, in vertex order, its first edge in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order (a self-loop covers its vertex). n − ν edges (Gallai)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(n · m · log n)."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumEdgeCover()"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()":{"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstmaximumindependentset()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first maximum independent set: of all the largest ones, the least by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Of two sets of one size, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference (the rule of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so on a loop-free graph this is that clique of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complement). A vertex with a self-loop is never in it; parallel edges count once.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalIndependentSet(containing:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalindependentset(containing:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A maximal independent set containing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seeds"},{"text":", which go in first, then each vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order as ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximalIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; nil when ","type":"text"},{"code":"seeds","type":